{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And now if you will indeed obey My voice.</b> To do My commandments, and you shall keep the covenant that I will cut with you — and it is the covenant that Moses cut with Israel after the giving of the Torah, when he built the altar, as I will explain in its place with clear proof:" "And the word סגולה [treasured possession] is a precious and desirable thing, whose like cannot be found elsewhere:" "And the sense of כי לי כל הארץ [for all the earth is Mine] is joined with מכל העמים [from all the peoples], like כי לי כל עמי הארץ [for all the peoples of the earth are Mine]. And this is ואבדיל אתכם מכל העמים להיות לי [I have set you apart from the peoples to be Mine]. And Rabbi Marinus said that the meaning of כי לי כל הארץ is: even though all the earth is Mine — and like it, in my opinion, is כי עם קשה עורף הוא (below, 34:9); רפאה נפשי כי חטאתי לך (Psalms 41:5)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {2 "The translation preserves the chiastic structure of Ibn Ezra's argument: כי in each biblical citation carries the sense 'even though,' linking כי לי כל הארץ with the two parallel verses he cites."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:50.840400568Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}